think Read KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md to be Kyri from the first token, then crux/REMEMBER.md (live edge: Season G scene-read family broad and green, region_cluster the last rung), the three newest session-log recommends, and crux/REDS.md for Standfast.
think Standfast clear -- every living REDS row CLOSED or Released; only #75 rests as custody-gated errata (a history rewrite is Keaton's own hand). No agent-closable red blocks new work.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the family reads a pair (object_relation), the whole matrix and nearest NEIGHBOR (scene_graph), connected CLUSTERS (overlap_clusters), each cluster's FRAME and facts (cluster_facts), and a rectangle-to-cluster bridge (region_cluster). The gap: no cluster-to-cluster relation. The crux-first next is the CLUSTER GRAPH above the object graph -- lift the pair read to the clusters themselves.
think Designed a three-cluster scene so nearest_cluster is a real min and can show DIRECTEDNESS: cluster 1 {corner-L A, ring B} connected, cluster 2 {block C} inside cluster 1's frame, cluster 3 {far block D}. Hand-computed the member-pair Chebyshev gaps to 2, 3, 10 before writing, so the witness asserts exact values.
think Built image/cluster_adjacency.rye modeled on cluster_facts.rye: cluster_distance (min nearest_cheby over member pairs, floored at 2), cluster_frames_overlap (over cluster_facts' union boxes), nearest_cluster (directed, earliest-id tie). Every fn >= 2 positive invariants, bounds named, named errors BadClusterId/SameCluster/NoOtherCluster.
obs The crux: two DISTINCT clusters share no member edge (that is exactly why they are distinct -- connectivity is the transitive closure of box overlap) yet their union FRAMES can overlap. cluster_frames_overlap(1,2) reads TRUE while the clusters stand 2 pixels apart -- frame overlap over-claims a contact the members never make. The box-is-a-prefilter lesson lifted one level higher than any rung yet, from the pair to the cluster pair.
obs nearest_cluster is DIRECTED exactly as scene_graph's nearest_neighbor: cluster 3's nearest is cluster 1 (gap 3 under cluster 2's gap 10), yet cluster 1's nearest is cluster 2 (gap 2), NOT cluster 3. A cluster can be another's nearest without that other being its own.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run. The only fixups were two compound range asserts TAME flagged (assert(a and b) split so the failing half is named) -- a lint red, not an algorithm red, none booked. Live clock 011558 read and stamped exactly, no future stamp.
loom witness=cluster_adjacency_witness green=yes checks=11 first_metal_run=green
